<!-- STEAM WORKSHOP (GAME MANAGER's DOWNLOAD FROM STEAM, its third row; the settings panel's Steam Workshop row in any
Menu style): Halo: MCC's Steam Workshop items for Halo CE, browsed and downloaded on the Vita through the player's own
Steam sign-in (port/steamdl, docs/steam_download_security.md sections 7-9). The Halo 3 / ElDewrito look: the navy
see-through panel, cards a lighter navy, the orange bar and frame on the focused card and tab.

First the notice and SIGN IN, then the QR for the Steam app (drawn over the panel's right side, menu_functions.c
h3_steam_qr_draw), then the browser: four tabs (POPULAR, NEWEST, TOP RATED, SUBSCRIBED - what the player subscribed
to on a PC or the Steam app, read only), L and R between them; a page of eight cards, four by two (the item's
picture, title, author, size, CAMPAIGN or MULTIPLAYER, its rating), the D-pad or the left stick between them, past
the edge to the next or the last page; a finger taps a card or a tab, swipes a page. Cross opens a card's details
page (its large picture - Left and Right through its pictures -, its description - Up and Down -, the maps it holds,
when it was updated, whether it is installed: Cross downloads or updates it, Triangle (twice) removes it). Square
marks a card (several for one download), Start downloads the marked ones, Triangle searches; Circle leaves a details
page, signs out of the list, or cancels a download (it resumes next time). Then the progress, the install (every map
checked by the game's own map check) and the end (signed out of Steam). The pictures, the frames and the rating's
pips are drawn over the cards by menu_functions.c (h3_workshop_draw); the text is its "port h3 workshop". -->
